ges (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(3))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4003-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507","date":"2026-05-07","original_code":"746.4003(a)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"First Aid Kit - Incomplete Kit: First aid kits on 2 of the 3 vehicles used were incomplete. Both were missing antiseptic solution and one did not have a working thermometer.    NOTE: Corrected at inspection All items were placed in the first aid kit","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026252171","violation_type_title":"First Aid Kit - Incomplete Kit (26 TAC §746.4003(a))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5607-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507","date":"2026-05-07","original_code":"746.5607(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-19","finding":"Child Passenger Safety Seat System - Not expired or damaged in accident: 15 child safety seats were observed to be expired on 3 of the vans used to transport children.  1 car seat with back, expired 2015. 14 booster seats between 2013 and 2022.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026413029","violation_type_title":"Child Passenger Safety Seat System - Not expired or damaged in accident (26 TAC §746.5607(b))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2207-c-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507","date":"2026-05-07","original_code":"746.2207(c)(3)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-19","finding":"Screen Time Activities - Not Exceed One Hour Daily: Upon arrival, at 6:49 children were observed watchinig tv. Children were still observed watching tv for the duation of the inspection until the last child left at 8:51pm, exceeding the one hr limit for screentime.","topic":"records","source_record_id":"1026292273","violation_type_title":"Screen Time Activities - Not Exceed One Hour Daily (26 TAC §746.2207(c)(3))","topic_label":"Records, permits & program"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2207-c-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507","date":"2026-05-07","original_code":"746.2207(c)(1)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-19","finding":"Screen Time Activities - Related to Planned Activities: Screen time was not observed to be related to a planned activity on the written plan.     NOTE: None of the activities written on the plan included screentime.","topic":"records","source_record_id":"1026373023","violation_type_title":"Screen Time Activities - Related to Planned Activities (26 TAC §746.2207(c)(1))","topic_label":"Records, permits & program"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1116810-i20260507","date":"2026-05-07","original_code":"746.1201(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-19","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children: During the duration of the inspection, caregivers were heard from another room loudly telling children to be quite and watch tv. At one point during the inspection, a caregiver was heard telling a child to be quiet then continued by stating\" you talk, talk talk,talk talk too much.\" The caregiver \"shushed\" the child then used their fingers to gesture to the child to zip their lips twice. Later, the caregiver was heard \"shushing\" children again putting their finger on their lip and telling children to be quiet.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026252172","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities 